# Jira ticket comments (Qatin)

Whenever any agent reads or analyzes a Jira ticket, **include the ticket comments**, not only summary/description.

## Why

Developers frequently leave testing guidance in comments: endpoints, payload shape, sample IDs, environment, caveats, and “how to verify”.

## Rules

1. Prefer concrete how-to-test notes from comments over invented assumptions.
2. Use comment facts for surface detection, acceptance criteria mining, case design, and explanations to the user.
3. If comments conflict with the description, call out the conflict; do not silently ignore the comment.
4. Paste-mode tickets have no comments — that is fine; do not invent them.
